<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Michael Shishman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1330</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Michael Asen III</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Michael Shishman was tsar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> from 1323 to 1330 and founder of the Shishman dynasty, the last ruling house of medieval Bulgaria. Previously despot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidin">Vidin</a>, he was elected by the boyars, fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> and later allied with Andronikos III. He was defeated and mortally wounded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-velbazhd">Battle of Velbazhd</a> in 1330.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/michael-shishman.jpg" alt="Michael Shishman" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Michael_Shishman.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
